# Every value here has a working default — the API boots with no configuration,
# and the web app builds with none.

# Where the app is published. Read when the web app is BUILT, not at runtime:
# it is the link the Share page sends, what its QR code encodes, and what the
# link-preview tags in index.html point at (apps/web/vite.site.ts). The deploy
# workflow's post-deploy check reads it back out of the build, so this and the
# default in apps/web/vite.config.ts are the only places the production address
# is written down. Absolute, with the trailing
# slash; anything that is not a URL fails the build rather than printing a QR
# code for a typo. On Vercel, set it in the project's environment variables.
SITE_URL=https://susanin.mnatsakanov.dev/

# Where the API listens (local / self-hosted only; Vercel sets this itself).
PORT=8787

# Browsers allowed to call the API cross-origin. Leave this UNSET: the web app
# is same-origin wherever it runs — deployed it shares a domain with the API,
# and in dev Vite proxies /api — so no browser here ever makes a cross-origin
# request. The two defaults exist for the packaged app alone, which serves its
# bundle from https://localhost (Android) or capacitor://localhost (iOS) and
# cannot be proxied.
#
# Setting this REPLACES the defaults rather than adding to them, so carry those
# two across or the APK goes blank. The one case that needs an entry of its own
# is pointing a browser straight at this port instead of through the proxy:
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,https://localhost,capacitor://localhost

# The Batumi feed's origin. The only reason to change it is the emergency
# fallback described in docs/data-source.md:
#   UPSTREAM_BASE=https://bus-proxy.raf003771.workers.dev
UPSTREAM_BASE=https://thetamaps.site:54321

# Upstream request budget, milliseconds. The dataset is 1.27 MB uncompressed,
# so this is not as generous as it looks.
UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# Cache lifetimes. These mirror what upstream itself asks for
# (`max-age=600` on the dataset, `max-age=4` on positions) — polling faster
# than the source updates only costs someone else's bandwidth.
DATASET_TTL_MS=600000
VEHICLES_TTL_MS=4000
